 molecular epidemiologic factors</article-title><source>Clin Infect Dis</source><volume>34</volume><fpage>752</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11850859</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b57-copd-2-263"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Palwatwichai</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Chaoprasong</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Vattanathum</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Clinical, laboratory findings and microbiologic characterization of bronchiectasis in Thai patients</article-title><source>Respirology</source><volume>7</volume><fpage>63</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11896903</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b58-copd-2-263"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Na</surname><given-names>JO</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>EK</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>The prognosis of respiratory failure in patients with tuberculous destroyed lung</article-title><source>Int J Tuberc Lung Dis</source><volume>5</volume><fpage>963</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11605892</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b59-copd-2-263"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pauwels</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Buist</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Calverley</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Global strategy for the diagnosis, management, and prevention of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. NHLBI/WHO Global Initiative for Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease (GOLD)